.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-scan 1  "dfdu-scan " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-scan \- Scan a directory and print a summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu scan\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-apparent\fR] [\fB\-\-like\-du\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-measure\-workers\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-rules\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-by\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-errors\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-history\fR] [\fB\-\-stall\-abandon\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a directory and print a summary
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output: table (for people), json (one document, schema/scan.v1.json), ndjson (one record per line, for large trees) or ncdu (ncdu\*(Aqs JSON export)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
ndjson
.IP \(bu 2
ncdu
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR
Levels of directories to print below the root [default: 1; every level for ndjson]
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR
Entries to print per directory, largest first [default: 10; all for ndjson]
.TP
\fB\-\-apparent\fR
Show apparent sizes instead of disk usage
.TP
\fB\-\-like\-du\fR
Count data shared between files (btrfs snapshots, reflinks, APFS clones) once per file, as du does, instead of once
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads for the scanned filesystem. Mounts below it with their own limit (spinning disks: 2, network: 4) add that many
.TP
\fB\-\-measure\-workers\fR \fI<MEASURE_WORKERS>\fR
Threads measuring shared extents (btrfs, XFS; APFS clones of 1 MiB or more); 0 reports sizes as du does
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rules\fR
Do not classify entries: no categories, no cleanup candidates
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fI<TYPES>\fR
Count only files of these types or extensions, comma\-separated: `video,audio,.iso`. Types: video, audio, image, document, archive, disk\-image, code, executable, font, data, other. Folders show the size of the matching files inside them
.TP
\fB\-\-by\-type\fR
After the tree, print disk usage by file type and the largest extensions
.TP
\fB\-\-bytes\fR
Print only the root total in bytes (for scripts and tests)
.TP
\fB\-\-errors\fR
List every entry that could not be read, with the reason
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-history\fR
Do not record the scan in the history (`dfdu diff`, `dfdu history`)
.TP
\fB\-\-stall\-abandon\fR \fI<STALL_ABANDON>\fR [default: 30]
Abandon directories stalled this many seconds
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

